## 2026-07-22 - Phase 15.7.1 validation isolation hardening

- Diagnosed the closure validation failure as a test-isolation defect: `workflowConditionSelfTest.js` imported the full database-backed `workflowExecutorService.js`, causing `packages/db/src/connection.js` to require `PGHOST` before the pure condition assertions began.
- Extracted condition normalization, typed-value parsing, path resolution, evaluation, and branch selection into dependency-free `apps/api/src/services/workflowConditionService.js`.
- Extracted the shared `WorkflowServiceError` class into `apps/api/src/services/workflowServiceError.js`, preserving one error identity across the pure condition service and production executor.
- Updated `workflowConditionSelfTest.js` to import the pure service directly, so it runs without `.env`, PostgreSQL, Axios, authentication, or Temporal bootstrap.
- Extended `phase15:closure-readiness:self-test` to prevent regression back to the full executor and to reject runtime dependency imports in the pure condition service.
- Added syntax checks for both new service modules to `npm run validate`.
- Production workflow behavior is unchanged; no migration, seed, dependency, tool registration, or workflow-definition update is required.
## 2026-07-23 - Phase 15.7.2 Human Approval parameter regression hotfix

- Fixed the Development Promotion Human Approval creation failure `ReferenceError: isBlankValue is not defined` introduced when condition logic was extracted from the database-backed workflow executor.
- Added dependency-free `workflowParameterUtils.js` as the single blank/optional-value normalizer used by CONDITION, WAIT, and HUMAN_APPROVAL parameter processing.
- Added `workflow-node-parameters:self-test` to verify blank-value semantics and assert that WAIT and Human Approval timeout parsing remain wired to the shared helper.
- Extended `phase15:closure-readiness:self-test` and `npm run validate` with the new regression coverage.
- No migration, seed, dependency, workflow-definition, or approval-ledger change is required. Restart the API and Temporal worker, then rerun Development Promotion from the beginning.


